---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Section from '../components/CitiesSection.astro';
---

<Layout title="Cities | Japanerary">
    <div class="my-6 px-10">
        <h1 class="text-4xl text-center font-bold">Cities</h1>

        <Section title="Tokyo" img="/public/tokyo-shinsaibashi.jpg" imgalt="Photograph of Tokyo, Japan night skyline">
            <p class="my-2">We felt like this had to be first. So, let's just get this out of the way and start in the prefecture of Tokyo.</p>
            <p class="my-2">As the current capital of Japan, Tokyo was instated during the Meiji Restoration under Emperor Meiji in 1868-1869. It serves as the countries capital in governance and finance.</p>
            <p class="my-2">Tokyo prefecture can be broken into 23 wards, or districts. With some of the most popular and well known wards being: Shibuya, Shinjuku, Chiyoda, and Chuo.</p>
            <p class="my-2">Tokyo is well known for its endless architecture, its polite society, clean streets, advanced (but potentially confusing) public transportation, fun activities, and more food than you can eat in an entire lifetime.</p>
            <p class="mt-2">Things to do:</p>
            <div>
                <ul class="list-disc pl-5">
                    <li>Visit Sky Tree tower</li>
                    <li>Shopping in Ginza</li>
                </ul>
            </div>
        </Section>

        <Section title="Kyoto" img="public/kyoto-arch2.jpg" imgalt="Photograph of Kyoto's city and landscape">
            <p>A true icon of Japan. Popular due to its treasured and well kept history, featuring tantalizing shrines, beautiful landscapes, and welcoming locals. Kyoto stands its ground as one of Japans most important and iconic cities.</p>
        </Section> 

        <Section title="Nara" img="/public/nara-todaiji.jpg" imgalt="Photograph of Deer between grave markers in Nara, Japan">
            <p>First, deer. Second, temples. What more could you ask for? Nara is an awesome stop near both Kyoto and Osaka (more on Osaka later) that has become popular for its deer feeding.</p>
        </Section>

        <Section title="Osaka" img="/public/osaka-crab.jpg" imgalt="Photograph of walkable vendor street with a tower in the background in Osaka, Japan">
            <p>As previously mentioned, Osaka is what many consider another must-go destination when in Japan. Also known as "The Kitchen of Japan" for its delicious cuisine, there are many staple places and foods at this hot spot.</p>
        </Section>
    </div>
</Layout>
